# How the box gets its certificate and whether it checks HELIOS's.
# Uncomment one block.
#
# 1. A public DNS name with ports 80 and 443 reachable: leave this file as it
#    is; Caddy gets a Let's Encrypt certificate.
#
# 2. A private name: Caddy's own CA (give HELIOS its root as HELIOS_AI_CA).
# tls internal
#
# 3. Mutual TLS: only a client presenting a certificate signed by the MSSP's
#    CA (certs/helios-ca.pem, from make-certs.sh) gets a connection. Write
#    "tls internal {" instead of "tls {" for a private name.
# tls {
# 	client_auth {
# 		mode require_and_verify
# 		trust_pool file /etc/caddy/certs/helios-ca.pem
# 	}
# }
